# SussIt Engineering Rules

SussIt is an Australian mobile-first second-hand buying decision app.

Core principle:

AI identifies and explains.
Deterministic application code determines prices, scores and confidence.

Never allow an LLM to invent or calculate the fundamental valuation.

## V0 Audience

Australian second-hand buyers.

## V0 Categories

- iPhones
- PlayStation
- Xbox
- Nintendo Switch
- Meta Quest

MacBooks and cameras come later.

## Design

Use /docs/design as the visual source of truth.

Brand:
- #C6FF00 acid lime
- #111111 near black
- #FAF8F5 warm off-white
- dark surface around #101617

Design should feel:
- premium consumer fintech
- minimal
- modern
- youthful
- mobile-first

Avoid:
- gradients
- glassmorphism
- excessive shadows
- generic SaaS layouts
- AI sparkles
- cluttered dashboards

## Technical stack

- React
- TypeScript
- Vite
- Tailwind
- shadcn/ui
- Supabase
- Vercel
- OpenAI

## Architecture

Core valuation logic lives in:

src/lib/valuation/

Pricing sources implement a PricingProvider interface.

Never couple valuation logic directly to eBay.

## Product philosophy

Trust > fake precision.

When data is insufficient, return INSUFFICIENT_DATA.

Never fabricate:
- accessories
- product variants
- condition
- market prices
- seller claims
- confidence

Unknown values remain null.

Do not add features that were not requested.
